  "body": {
    "id": "lem:tight-moment-radius-forces-zero-means",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(q_0=4+\\delta\\). If the allowed primitive constants obey \\(v_{\\star}=v^{\\star}=v>0\\) and \\(M_{\\mathrm{mom}}=(2v)^{q_0/2}\\), then every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\) has \\(m_c=0\\) and \\(\\varepsilon_i=0\\) almost surely conditional on \\(C_i=c\\), for every \\(c\\). In particular, \\(\\mu(P)=0\\) throughout this allowed model class.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "delta",
      "vstar",
      "vupper",
      "Mmom",
      "P",
      "Mclass",
      "mload",
      "epsilon",
      "C",
      "mu"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:base-model"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(c\\) and put \\(q_0=4+\\delta>2\\). The two covariance bounds with equal endpoints give\n\\[\nH_c=vI_2.\n\\]\nBy the conditional moment-radius assumption, Lyapunov's inequality, and the identity \\(\\mathbb E_P\\|\\lambda_i\\|^2\\mid C_i=c=\\operatorname{tr}(H_c)+\\|m_c\\|^2\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2v)^{q_0/2}=M_{\\mathrm{mom}}\n&\\geq \\mathbb E_P\\!\\left[\\|\\lambda_i\\|^{q_0}+\\|\\varepsilon_i\\|^{q_0}\\mid C_i=c\\right]\\\\\n&\\geq \\mathbb E_P[\\|\\lambda_i\\|^{q_0}\\mid C_i=c]\\\\\n&\\geq \\left\\{\\mathbb E_P[\\|\\lambda_i\\|^2\\mid C_i=c]\\right\\}^{q_0/2}\\\\\n&=(2v+\\|m_c\\|^2)^{q_0/2}\\geq(2v)^{q_0/2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nAll inequalities are therefore equalities. Strict monotonicity of \\(x\\mapsto x^{q_0/2}\\) gives \\(m_c=0\\), and equality in the first line gives \\(\\mathbb E_P[\\|\\varepsilon_i\\|^{q_0}\\mid C_i=c]=0\\), hence \\(\\varepsilon_i=0\\) almost surely conditional on the cohort. Finally the rank-two outcome equation and the conditional error-mean restriction give \\(\\mu_c(P)=\\Gamma m_c=0\\). The argument applies to every cohort.",
